Short cross-session narrative feed. **Rotated 2026-08-26**: this file had grown
to 3,438 lines / 484 KB, which is not a feed any reader scans -- it is an
append-only archive nobody reads. The prior entries are in git history
(`git log -p -- .agents/activity.log`) and are not lost.

Keep it short. If an entry matters beyond the next session it belongs in a
typed home instead: `docs/concerns/` for a finding, `openspec/changes/` for
work, memory for a durable lesson, the git log for what landed. This file is
for narrative that helps the next session orient and then stops mattering.

